
@startuml VoleMachineSimple

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide empty members

title Vole Machine Simulator - Four-Class Architecture

class Memory {
  - cells : uint8_t[256]
  - screenOutput : string

  + read(address : uint8_t) : uint8_t
  + write(address : uint8_t, value : uint8_t) : void
  + getCells() : const uint8_t*
  + getScreenOutput() : string
  + clear() : void
}

class CPU {
  - pc : uint8_t
  - ir : uint16_t
  - registers : uint8_t[16]
  - halted : bool
  - memory : Memory&

  + CPU(memory : Memory&)
  + step() : void
  + isValid(ir : uint16_t) : bool
  + getPC() : uint8_t
  + setPC(address : uint8_t) : void
  + getIR() : uint16_t
  + getRegister(index : uint8_t) : uint8_t
  + setRegister(index : uint8_t, value : uint8_t) : void
  + isHalted() : bool

  - fetch() : bool
  - execute() : void
}

class Machine {
  - memory : Memory
  - cpu : CPU
  - programStart : uint8_t

  + loadProgram(filename : string, startAddress : uint8_t) : bool
  + run() : void
  + runStep() : bool

  + getPC() : uint8_t
  + getIR() : uint16_t
  + getRegister(index : uint8_t) : uint8_t
  + getRegisters() : const uint8_t*
  + getMemoryCell(address : uint8_t) : uint8_t
  + getMemoryCells() : const uint8_t*
  + getScreenOutput() : string
  + isHalted() : bool

  + overwriteRegister(index : uint8_t, value : uint8_t) : void
  + overwriteMemory(address : uint8_t, value : uint8_t) : void
  + setPCToStart() : void
}

class UI {
  + start() : void

  - showMenu() : void
  - displayMemory() : void
  - displayRegisters() : void
  - displayScreen() : void
}

Machine "1" *-- "1" Memory : owns
Machine "1" *-- "1" CPU : owns

CPU "1" --> "1" Memory : reads / writes

UI "1" --> "1" Machine : uses Facade

note right of Memory
  Memory capacity: 256 bytes (0x00-0xFF).

  Address 0xFF is the screen output port.
  Writing to 0xFF synchronizes screenOutput
  with the written byte.

  clear() resets all cells and screenOutput.

  getCells() returns a read-only pointer
  to the internal memory array.
end note

note right of CPU
  Instruction fetch:
  1. Validate PC and PC + 1.
  2. Read two consecutive bytes.
  3. Combine them into a 16-bit IR.
  4. Advance PC by 2 only after a valid fetch.

  Prevent out-of-bounds access and
  unintended address wraparound.

  step() fetches and executes one instruction
  unless the CPU is halted or fetch fails.
end note

note right of Machine
  Machine is the public Facade for UI.

  Loading validation:
  - startAddress must be even.
  - startAddress must be < 0xFF.
  - The entire program must fit in memory.
  - Reject invalid input before modifying memory.

  runStep() delegates one execution step.
  run() executes until halt or a defined
  execution failure condition.

  getRegisters() and getMemoryCells()
  expose read-only views for rendering.
end note

note right of UI
  UI communicates only through Machine.

  Responsibilities:
  - Menu and user input.
  - Memory matrix rendering.
  - Register and PC/IR display.
  - Screen output display.

  No direct access to CPU or Memory.
end note

@enduml